# PlatformBox design system

## Brand positioning

Ultra-premium B2B SaaS for Fractional CTOs. Visual north stars: **Linear.app** and **Vercel** — strict dark mode, high signal, low noise.

## Visual tokens

| Token | Direction |
| --- | --- |
| Background | Zinc-950 / near-black charcoal |
| Text | White headings, zinc-400 body |
| Accent | Electric blue (CTA, links, icon accents) — not purple |
| Borders | `border-white/10` glass edges |
| Radius | Subtle (`rounded-lg` / `rounded-xl`), not pill-heavy |
| Type | Geist / tight tracking on headlines |

CSS variables live in `src/app/globals.css`. Extend there first.

## Landing composition

1. **Hero** — brand, one H1, one supporting sentence, CTA pair, atmospheric grid/glow. No stats strips, promo chips, or card clutter in the first viewport.
2. **Problem** — one job: name the bottleneck.
3. **Deliverables** — 2×2 glass bento; icon + title + short text.
4. **Economics** — ROI list + distinct investment card (`$20,000 USD` / `14 Days`).
5. **Footer** — minimal: copyright, email, LinkedIn.

## UX rules

- One purpose per section; one headline; usually one short supporting line.
- Primary CTA: solid accent. Secondary: outline / low-contrast glass.
- Cards only when they group interactive or scannable deliverables — not around the hero.
- Motion: 2–3 intentional entrance patterns sitewide; professional, not playful.
- Fully responsive: stacked CTAs and single-column grids on small screens.

## Copy

- Use the approved product copy already on the page unless the user provides new copy.
- Do not invent testimonials, fake logos, or unverifiable metrics.
- Keep currency/pricing strings consistent with the source of truth on the page (`$20,000 USD`, € figures in ROI bullets as written).

## Icons

- Lucide, stroke-consistent, modest size (`h-4` / `h-5`).
- Place icons in a small bordered well for deliverable cards.
- If a Lucide brand icon is missing, use a minimal inline SVG.
